# Daily Project Update Tracker

File: `Aryabangi_Motors_Daily_Project_Update_Tracker (1).xlsx`  
Sheet: `Daily Work Log`

## When to update

- At the end of a working session, or when the user asks to update the tracker / log today’s work.
- Do this **every working day** there was project progress — same habit as prior days (e.g. 16–17 Nov entries).
- If the user is mid-task and did not ask, do not interrupt; update when they wrap up or ask.

## How to write the row

Match the existing columns and tone of prior rows (especially the latest dated entry):

| Column | Content |
|--------|---------|
| Date | Today’s date |
| Day | Leave the existing `=IF(A…,"",TEXT(A…,"dddd"))` formula |
| Work ID | Next integer (or reuse same ID if continuing one open thread) |
| Module / Area | Short theme for the day’s work |
| Task / Requirement | One-line goal |
| Work Done by Me | Short numbered bullets only — one line each, no long explanation |
| Result / Output | What works / was measured / delivered |
| Status | Usually `In Progress` until client closes items; use dropdown values |
| Pending From Client | `yes` / `no` as appropriate |
| Additional Notes | Open client questions, caveats |

Do not invent client messages/replies. Leave those blank unless they happened.

## After writing

- Save the xlsx in place (same filename).
- Briefly tell the user the row date/Work ID was added.
- Prefer editing via openpyxl (or equivalent) so formulas and other sheets stay intact.
